nina_sales: Eve at CartWave wants a short pilot: streaming responses that trigger tool/function calls and must return strict JSON per-tenant. Needs SAML SSO, KMS/BYOK guidance, a 1-pager runbook for infra, and a pricing ballpark for a 90-day pilot (~5M tokens/day, peak ~50 rps). Can we list blockers and the minimal artifacts to hand them?
eve_cust: yep. also want an SDK sample we can drop into our staging (prefer Node), and a note on reconnect behavior and how to surface schema validation failures to our app.
omar_se: Plan: 1) Hosted demo for first pass; Dedicated if they need latency SLAs or stronger isolation. 2) Provide Node SDK websocket example + a tiny test harness to assert JSON schema conformance. 3) One-page runbook for ephemeral token flow + reconnect. 4) Pricing: hosted pilot blended cap OR Dedicated trial commit.
paul_prod: Security highlights to include: TLS 1.3, AES-256 at rest, BYOK supported for Private deployments, configurable audit logs, SOC2 summary available. I'll attach short FAQ.
security_bot: Security questionnaire and SOC2 excerpt uploaded to secure link (sales+sec): https://redwood.internal/sq/cartwave-3501234567 :lock:
sophie_infra: Handshake/runbook notes: prefer WebSocket for low-latency streaming. Recommend ephemeral token TTL 1h for POC; rotate tokens by reconnect every ~45 minutes. Avoid swapping tokens mid-stream. Backpressure: client applies rate-limits and graceful drain on reconnect. Provide sample curl/wscat and a tiny reconnect state machine snippet.
omar_se: Node SDK sample for them to copy/paste (stream + function_call + structured output). Use structured_output and include JSON schema:```js
const Redwood = require('redwood-sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const ws = client.stream({ model: 'redwood-chat-1', structured_output: true, schema: { type: 'object', properties: { tenant_id: { type: 'integer' }, items: { type: 'array' } }, required: ['tenant_id', 'items'] } });
ws.send({ input: 'Summarize orders for tenant=7', functions: [ { name: 'fetch_orders', schema: { type: 'object', properties: { tenant_id: { type: 'integer' } }, required: ['tenant_id'] } } ] });
ws.on('message', async (ev) => {
  if (ev.type === 'function_call') {
    const res = await localFetchOrders(ev.args);
    ws.send({ function_response: res });
  } else if (ev.type === 'chunk') {
    process.stdout.write(ev.text);
  } else if (ev.type === 'validation_error') {
    console.error('schema validation failed:', ev.errors);
    // surface to monitoring/alerting
  }
});
```
eve_cust: can you show the ephemeral token handshake too? we need to rotate automatically from our auth bridge.
sophie_infra: Handshake example (minimal):```bash
# request ephemeral token from your auth service
curl -X POST https://auth.cartwave.example/ephemeral -d '{"service":"cartwave-poc"}' | jq -r .token
# connect via wscat
wscat -c "wss://stream.redwood.ai/v1/chat?token=<EPHEMERAL>"
```
sophie_infra: Rotation pattern: background timer requests new token at T-15min, open new socket, wait for in-flight requests to finish (or drain window), then swap. Avoid interrupting active function calls.
paul_prod: Pricing note for sales: propose two paths in the quote: Hosted pilot with capped blended rate for 90 days; Dedicated trial with monthly commit showing lower per-token unit cost. Include an option to convert remaining pilot spend into a Reserved capacity credit.
omar_se: Potential blocker: if CartWave requires on-prem processing of regulated PII we need to schedule a Private deployment (6-8 week lead). Otherwise Hosted + BYOK + VPC egress covers most compliance needs. Call this out in the handoff.
ninja: (auto) demo environment provisioned: demo-cartwave-3501234567. Creds will be DM'd to participants.
security_bot: Note: recommend running appendix A.3 (SOC2 artifact check) before the demo if they asked for compliance docs.
paul_prod: Action items: Omar to post Node SDK sample and a small test harness by EOD; Sophie to publish the 1-pager runbook (handshake, rotation, failures); Paul attach security FAQ and SOC2 excerpt; Sales to collect SAML metadata and schedule demo (1.5h).
